# Secrets and settings for the Hermes director. This is a template only.
#
# The director is its own Hermes profile, `director`, with its own .env file:
#   Windows:        %LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes\profiles\director\.env
#   Linux / macOS:  ~/.hermes/profiles/director/.env
# (`hermes profile show director` prints the folder.) Set the values with
# `hermes -p director config set NAME value`, which writes that file for you.
# Never commit real values.

# The director's own model, from any provider Hermes supports (Nous Portal, OpenRouter,
# OpenAI, Google Gemini, DeepSeek, ...). Hermes does not use Claude. Run
# `hermes -p director model`: it signs you in, or asks for the provider's key and
# writes it here under the provider's own name, for example:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Telegram, to talk to Hermes from your phone and to receive the scheduled reports.
# `hermes -p director gateway setup` asks for these.
# 1. Create a bot with @BotFather and paste its token. A bot token works in one
#    Hermes profile only: do not put it in the default profile too.
# 2. Send /start to @userinfobot to get your numeric user id.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=
TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL=

# Optional: one Hostinger API token per Hostinger account, for the Hostinger MCP
# servers (reboot from outside, snapshots, metrics). See docs/home/hostinger-api.md.
HOSTINGER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_1=
HOSTINGER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_2=
HOSTINGER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_3=
HOSTINGER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_4=
HOSTINGER_TOKEN_ACCOUNT_5=
